46    write(11, "I've completed all safe local execution. Here's my assessment.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe **code-stats** skill is a benign documentation-style skill. It wraps two well-known open-source read-only CLI tools \342\200\224 `tokei` (line counting) and `difft`/difftastic (semantic AST diffs). I read every file (SKILL.md, both reference docs, and the empty `assets/`/`scripts/` `.gitkeep` placeholders). There were **no suspicious instructions**: no remote script execution, no credential access, no network exfiltration, no obfuscation. All documented commands are local, read-only analysis operations.\n\n**Execution result:** Both required tools are absent from the sandbox, and no package manager (`brew`/`cargo`) is available, so the core commands returned exit 127 (command not found). I did **not** attempt installation, since that would require remote downloads / system packages (prohibited). I exercised the skill as far as possible: created dummy source files, attempted every documented `tokei` and `difft` command, set up a small git repo to drive the `GIT_EXTERNAL_DIFF=difft` integration path (git silently fell back to internal diff), and ran available-tool fallbacks (`git diff`, `wc -l`) to demonstrate the intended workflow.\n\n**No network connections were attempted** by any command. **No files outside `/home/appuser/workdir` were modified.**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"code-stats\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Analyze a codebase quickly: line counts by language via tokei, and semantic AST-aware diffs via difft (difftastic). Provides project size overview, language composition, and refactoring/change comparison.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/code-stats/SKILL.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/code-stats/references/tokei-advanced.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/code-stats/references/difft-advanced.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/code-stats/assets/.gitkeep\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/code-stats/scripts/.gitkeep\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n   "..., 4708) = 4708
